# What this plugin will not do

One entry, and it is the list of what survives the plugin being removed rather
than a single claim. Two of its three kinds say which of the two states they are
in and the one about the configuration does not, so the entry passes the leg
that asks the question once per heading on a marker belonging to a different
kind. Recorded in #57 so the leg about issues is not the one that trips.

## What removing the plugin does not delete

Removing the plugin removes its configuration and its records, because those are
plugin data and the server removes plugin data.

Temporary audio is already gone for a run that ended, and what a process that
died mid-run left behind is collected by nothing, which is decided and not yet
built. #11 and #21.

Generated subtitle files stay on disk, and this plugin has no removal path that
would take one away. Held today. #43.

## When this list is checked against the code

The closing section, which is about the list rather than a limit in it.
